0000000000003},{"ratio":0.99,"watchRatio":0.3969},{"ratio":1,"watchRatio":0.3908}],"script":{"source_path":"2026-11-madhavrao-reel3-rakshasbhuvan.md","words":247,"wpm":null,"lang":"en","chapters":[],"blocks":[{"sec":0,"text":"The Nizam of Hyderabad had sacked Pune."},{"sec":2.4,"text":"He thought Maratha Empire was finished,"},{"sec":4.1,"text":"but he had one more obstacle, the"},{"sec":5.8,"text":"18-year-old Peshwa Madhavrao. Just"},{"sec":7.8,"text":"months earlier, Madhavrao's uncle,"},{"sec":9.8,"text":"Raghunathrao, had snatched his throne."},{"sec":11.8,"text":"His persecution of Madhavrao's"},{"sec":13.2,"text":"supporters had driven thousands of"},{"sec":15.2,"text":"Maratha soldiers into Nizam's camp. Now,"},{"sec":17.6,"text":"the Nizam's minister, Vitthal Sundar,"},{"sec":19.5,"text":"was leading a campaign to destroy the"},{"sec":21.1,"text":"Maratha Empire. But Madhavrao had a"},{"sec":23,"text":"plan. Following his grandfather"},{"sec":24.6,"text":"Bajirao's strategy, he took the fight"},{"sec":26.6,"text":"deep into Nizam's territory and secretly"},{"sec":28.8,"text":"won back many of commanders who had"},{"sec":30.3,"text":"deserted him. Then on August 10th, 1763,"},{"sec":33.3,"text":"the Nizam crossed the flooded Godavari"},{"sec":35.6,"text":"with half his army, leaving Vitthal"},{"sec":37.4,"text":"Sundar and the main force [music] at"},{"sec":39,"text":"Rakshasbhuvan. The Marathas attacked."},{"sec":41.1,"text":"The battle was fierce. Raghunathrao's"},{"sec":43.5,"text":"elephant was surrounded. His life was in"},{"sec":45.4,"text":"danger. Maratha soldiers were"},{"sec":47,"text":"retreating, but Madhavrao saw his uncle"},{"sec":49.1,"text":"in danger. He turned his horse and"},{"sec":51,"text":"charged straight into enemy ranks."},{"sec":52.8,"text":"Fighting his way through rescue of the"},{"sec":54.2,"text":"very uncle who had taken his throne,"},{"sec":56.3,"text":"humiliated him. Seeing their young"},{"sec":58,"text":"Peshwa charge, the Maratha soldiers"},{"sec":60.1,"text":"turned around and followed him. The"},{"sec":61.6,"text":"retreat became an attack. Vitthal Sundar"},{"sec":64,"text":"was killed. His army was crushed. The"},{"sec":66.1,"text":"Nizam could only watch from across the"},{"sec":67.7,"text":"river. Madhavrao saved his uncle and"},{"sec":70.2,"text":"rallied an army that was on [music]"},{"sec":71.7,"text":"verge of defeat. The Nizam was forced to"},{"sec":73.7,"text":"sign the treaty. Madhavrao had saved the"},{"sec":75.7,"text":"empire [music] and proved he was worthy"},{"sec":77.5,"text":"of the throne his uncle had taken from"},{"sec":79.1,"text":"him."}],"text":""}}